%description:

Tcp.ecnWillingness:off -- tcpEcnMode decides: the SYN of the default "passive" requests no ECN.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "deprecated: true is tcpEcnMode="rfc3168", in place of "off" or
"passive"".

The classes: off (false, the default: tcpEcnMode decides), on (true: "rfc3168" in place of
"off" or "passive"), conflict (true with a tcpEcnMode that requests ECN: an error). The code:
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables(). This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host1, with the default tcpEcnMode. Observation: level 1, the SYN of host1 has
no ECN bits.

%# parameter: Tcp.ecnWillingness
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.ecnWillingness
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpEcnWillingnessOff")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.aeBit == false && tcp.cwrBit == false && tcp.eceBit == false")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpEcnWillingnessOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.ecnWillingness = false    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpEcnWillingnessOff: PASS
